1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Natalia Pavlovna Paley'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nathalie_Paley
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7187149/natalia_pavlovna
2 CONT
2 CONT Russian Royalty. The first cousin of Tsar Nicholas II, she was the daughter of Grand Duke Paul Alexandrovich by his second wife Princess Olga Paley. When she was still a young girl she had to escape from Russia due to the Revoluti
2 CONC on ''(her father and her brother Vladimir were murdered by the Bolsheviks)'' and went to France with her mother and sister. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1927 she married Lucien-Camille Lelong, a talented French fashion designer and also a war hero, but had no issue and divorced him in 1937. After working for a while as a fashion model for her husband enterprises and appearing s
2 CONC everal times in "Vogue," she became a movie actress and was in several European movies, including Sir Alexander Korda's ''"The Private Life of Don Juan"'' (1931) and "Marcel L'Herbier "L'épervier" (1933). 
2 CONT
2 CONT She eventually moved to the United States, acted in George Cukor's "Sylvia Scarlett" (1935) and began a close intimate friendship with the film's main star, Katherine Hepburn, which would last all through her life. After charming 
2 CONC spectators with her beauty and experiencing a brief success, she quit acting, married in 1937 the theatre producer John Chapman Wilson and settled with him in Manhattan, where for many years she worked in public relations for the 
2 CONC fashion designer Mainbocher.
