1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hubert de Monbrison was born in 1892 in Saint-Avertin (Indre-et-Loire) into a French-Irish Protestant family.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his studies, he left as a lumberjack and herdsman on a ranch in Nevada (USA).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1914, he returned to France and ended the war with various military rewards.
2 CONT
2 CONT After this conflict, he supported conscientious objectors, joined social Christianity, and met Pastor Henri Roser * and André Philip *.
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 3, 1939, the Count de Monbrison , General Secretary of the Rescue for the Children of Political Refugees, put at the disposal of the OSE for a group of forty boys from Berlin, Quincy-sous-Sénart castle which already housed
2 CONC  a few young people. Russian girls emigrated in 1917 and Spanish refugee girls.
2 CONT
2 CONT []https://collections.ushmm.org/search/catalog/irn1004611 From his marriage with a Jew, he will have four children, who will be educated at the College Cevennes from 1942.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1950s, he moved to an agricultural estate in Tarn-et-Garonne where he founded one of the first dairy cooperatives in the southwest, Tempé-Lait in Montauban.
