1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This mariage contract establishes the link between Lazare Salomon Levy and Salomon Düsseldorf Levy
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Number, Page, and Number: 1886 Page p 165 Marriage No. 3
2 CONT Notary: OBERNAI
2 CONT Date and Place of Contract: December 2, 1751 in OBERNAI
2 CONT Groom's First and Last Name: GOUDCHAUX LEVY
2 CONT Born in: METZ
2 CONT Groom's Father's First and Last Name: LAZARE SALOMON LEVY Deceased
2 CONT Groom's Mother's First and Last Name: BEYLE
2 CONT Comments Concerning the Groom: Father-in-law: Moyse Isaac Spire Levy, banker from Metz, born around 1735, died on January 31, 1795 (Ros)
2 CONT Bride's First and Last Name: HENDLE WEYL
2 CONT Born in: OBERNAI
2 CONT Bride's Father's First and Last Name: JACOB WEYL
2 CONT Bride's Paternal Grandfather's First and Last Name: BAROUCH WEYL
2 CONT Mother's First and Last Name From the bride: MERLE CAHEN
2 CONT
2 CONT The groom offers gifts valued at 3,500 pounds. He brings the inheritance he received from his grandfather, Salomon Lévy, a banker in Hanover.
2 CONT Dowry: 24,000 pounds.
2 CONT Ketuba: 36,000 pounds.
2 CONT Hebrew text signed by Moyse Nordon, rabbi in Rosheim, and Israel Bing, rabbi in Obemai.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mêmoire Juive en Alsace - André Fraenkel 
